---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { company, hqAddressLine } from '../data/company';
---

<LegalPage title="Privacy policy" description="How Incoltec processes the personal data collected through its website." heading="Privacy policy" updated="Last updated: November 2026">
  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Controller:</strong> {company.legalName} (INCOLTEC), Tax ID {company.taxId}</li>
    <li><strong>Address:</strong> {hqAddressLine}, Spain</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy contact:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> · {company.phone}</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What data we process, why, and on what legal basis</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Processing</th><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th><th>Retention</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Contact, sample and data-sheet form</td><td>Name, email, company, phone (optional), country, product and message; language and source page</td><td>To answer your enquiry and send documentation or samples</td><td>Your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR) and pre-contractual steps at your request (Art. 6(1)(b))</td><td>As long as needed to handle the enquiry, then up to 2 years or the applicable legal periods</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Commercial communications</td><td>Name, email and company</td><td>To send you information about products, news and events</td><td>Your consent, requested in a separate, unticked box</td><td>Until you withdraw consent</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Newsletter</td><td>Email</td><td>To send you our newsletter</td><td>Your consent</td><td>Until you unsubscribe</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Web analytics (only if you accept)</td><td>Pseudonymised browsing data</td><td>To understand how the site is used and improve it</td><td>Your consent via the cookie panel</td><td>See the <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie policy</a></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Fields marked as required are needed to handle your request. We do not make automated decisions or create profiles with legal effects.</p>

  <h2>3. Recipients and processors</h2>
  <p>We do not share your data with third parties unless legally required. To provide the service we use processors bound by contracts under Art. 28 GDPR: web hosting (Vercel Inc.), our corporate email provider and, where enabled, the analytics tool and the form's anti-spam service.</p>

  <h2>4. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Some providers, such as Vercel Inc., may process data outside the European Economic Area. Such transfers rely on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or on the European Commission's standard contractual clauses.</p>

  <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can exercise your rights of access, rectification, erasure, objection, restriction and portability, and withdraw consent at any time, by writing to <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> stating the right you wish to exercise. If you believe your request has not been handled properly, you may complain to the Spanish Data Protection Agency (<a href="https://www.aepd.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.aepd.es</a>).</p>

  <h2>6. Security</h2>
  <p>We apply appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your data, such as encrypted connections (HTTPS) and restricted access to information.</p>
</LegalPage>
